{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-15457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,y={cos}^{2}⁡(t),\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-15457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-15457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ff7195070194e94c62c16157f4145a9e13fd6b0215b65d959dea0c3e354b1bef"} {"question" "q-15457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-15457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "-\\,\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-15457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-15469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{3}+1,\\,y={t}^{4}+2{t}^{2},\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-15469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6{t}^{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=4t({t}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{4t({t}^{2}+1)}{6{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({t}^{2}+1)}{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2((1)^{2}+1)}{3\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-15469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ff7195070194e94c62c16157f4145a9e13fd6b0215b65d959dea0c3e354b1bef"} {"question" "q-15469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-15469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-15469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-102940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{2}+3,\\,y=3{t}^{5}+{t}^{3},\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-102940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}(5{t}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{3{t}^{2}(5{t}^{2}+1)}{4t}=\\frac{3t(5{t}^{2}+1)}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{3(1)(5(1)^{2}+1)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-102940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ff7195070194e94c62c16157f4145a9e13fd6b0215b65d959dea0c3e354b1bef"} {"question" "q-102940" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-102940" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{11}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{15}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-102940" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-353340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/assets/e0b1dc90950ba127e90fce400bc7ed1b6e8dd8e710ff880ab5949521b02a258a.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=4{e}^{-t},\\,y={t}^{2}+6t,\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}{|}_{t\\,=\\,1}=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-353340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-4{e}^{-t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t+6.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2t+6}{(-4{e}^{-t})}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}{|}_{t\\,=\\,1} & =\\frac{2(1)+6}{(-4{e}^{-1})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8e}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-2e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-353340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ff7195070194e94c62c16157f4145a9e13fd6b0215b65d959dea0c3e354b1bef"} {"question" "q-353340" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-353340" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2e"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-353347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{3t},\\,y=2{e}^{t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ as a function of $t.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-353347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{3t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{3{e}^{3t}}=\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-2t}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-353347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ff7195070194e94c62c16157f4145a9e13fd6b0215b65d959dea0c3e354b1bef"} {"question" "q-353347" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"} {"question" "q-353347" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}e^{-2t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/state.json" "file_sha256" "b62729155ed03f7b471ab92d703d9df7affc92e529c4865d18be757031a399e5"}] "usage" {} "basis" 858 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
